   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Intermediate Results Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">2. Share of tagged budget programs linked to Government&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x2122;s climate change priorities (percent of total)</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2022-12-15" value="Nil (2022)" year="2022">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN"></narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-12-15"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="1900-01-01"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">[Slow Progress] The implementation of climate budget tagging is slightly delayed due to staff changes within Government and late uptake of the reform post-election. Technical Assistance (TA) from UNDP is supporting the Government in developing a roadmap, revising budget call circulars, producing a working paper on methodology and options for revising the Chart of Accounts. Contingent on successful delivery of the TA together with the WB advisory and implementation support, the target is expected to be achieved by 2027.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="0"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
